{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Fin Central Channel Geometry.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Fin Central Channel Geometry.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"fin central channel geometry fin central channel geometry","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Fin Central Channel Geometry.md","fileName":"Fin Central Channel Geometry.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Fin Central Channel Geometry","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 00:45\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Parametric Fin Geometry]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Parametric Fin Geometry","geometrycreationandimport.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Fin Central Channel Geometry.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Fin Central Channel Geometry.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"fin central channel geometry fin central channel geometry","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Fin Central Channel Geometry.md","fileName":"Fin Central Channel Geometry.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Fin Central Channel Geometry","heading":"Fin Central Channel Geometry","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A fin central channel is a void created by subtracting an internal solid from the surrounding fin geometry. Its cross section and placement alter material volume, exposed surface, conduction paths, and the topology that must be meshed.\n\nThe subtracting object should be parameterized and aligned through explicit coordinates or a work plane. Measuring the completed channel and remaining tip features verifies that the Boolean difference produced the intended opening rather than an enclosed cavity or broken domain.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Parametric Fin Geometry","geometrycreationandimport.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Fin Central Channel Geometry.md::2","s